    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d635">

                <pb facs="0676" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5592: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-10-13T16:00:00+08:00">October 13, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received Octover 13—5:24 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1185. Department’s written instruction 856, September 2, reporting <pb
                        facs="0677" n="579" xml:id="pg579"/> conversation between Castle and Italian
                    Ambassador on August 25th.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d635-f1"/></p>
                <p>With reference to final paragraph of Castle’s memorandum I have discussed matter
                    with Military Attaché and he has made discreet inquiries among all other
                    Military Attachés who participated in discussions regarding neutralization of
                    Peiping and he reports that no such proposal was made by the head of the
                    Japanese Legation guard to any of the various Military Attachés on that
                    subject.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d635-f1" n="9" xml:id="d635-f1-content">
                <p>Instruction No. 856 not printed; it enclosed a copy of the memorandum of August
                    29, <ref target="#pg573">p. 573</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
